#: 1d4ce23033f64bd88b799d95e96123d6
msgid "Jittor Repository Layout"
msgstr "计图仓库布局"

#: 9a7d360b243f47fcbecd4b49b4d27392
msgid "Status: Accepted"
msgstr ""

#: fb6376005cfc43b395b477dcc99577ca
msgid "Date: 2026-08-11"
msgstr ""

#: 95fe2a201a72406abf3fba3381b20e6f
msgid ""
"Scope: Jittor 2.0 repository structure, packaging, compatibility "
"ownership, tests, tooling, and documentation"
msgstr ""

#: 08187abc1ae3425a96ddfcb350f67c6c
msgid ""
"Supersedes: the long-term `facade.py + _private/` target and the decision"
" to ship `jittor.test` as a public package"
msgstr ""

#: 84c53f1e15404d0e9d9fe37aed70bb0b
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: fbfb1cb5f59f45d59c8ad7c01edeb7be
msgid ""
"The repository grew from an upstream source tree by accumulating "
"compatibility layers, backend adapters, tests, release scripts, and "
"generated documentation. The resulting layout has three systemic "
"problems:"
msgstr ""

#: 8675b8fef9bb43e6957543b7fe241e08
msgid ""
"Packaging is not authoritative. A short explicit package list and "
"recursive `package_data` globs happen to place undeclared Python packages"
" in wheels, while deeper runtime resources can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: 39a682cd8c6542aaa8b430da8f4c18c5
msgid ""
"Domain modules use a public file plus a parallel `_domain/` "
"implementation package. Runtime proxies and rewritten `__module__` "
"metadata are then needed to work around the artificial boundary."
msgstr ""

#: b29d04f4707846928778061098ddc931
msgid ""
"Framework capability, reusable patching mechanisms, Jittor semantic "
"fixes, and downstream project glue are mixed in the Torch compatibility "
"layer."
msgstr ""

#: 88c90fe7c4f94c19a61b81f94c389094
msgid ""
"This RFC defines the end state. Earlier facade splits remain useful "
"migration work, but their private-package shape is transitional rather "
"than the target."
msgstr ""

#: 2061b952463741c3a3381e3d3bc488d0
msgid "Decision Baseline"
msgstr ""

#: a56cbae3e7ff4fa0a5783f5e2971ddd1
msgid ""
"At the time of this decision, commit `47e7ec75` contained source-refactor"
" batches 10 and 11. Its accepted evidence includes exact AST comparisons "
"for the moved miscellaneous functions, public identity and dynamic "
"dispatch tests, 79 FSDP2 public names, 70 callable contracts, 37 deep "
"distributed registrations, CPU/CUDA regression, and a real two-GPU NCCL "
"step. Those results remain the behavioral baseline while the temporary "
"package shape changes."
msgstr ""

#: 891bfe9e040a4d79b30dc5cecceabff9
msgid ""
"That wheel baseline had 1,053 entries and already contained "
"`UnpackRaw.cuh`; the packaging task was to make that resource explicit "
"and tested, not to claim it was missing. At that point, the deploy helper"
" still omitted `flash_attn_interface.py` when copying stubs into a "
"deployment tree."
msgstr ""

#: f4a01cb89a3a4a43bfa913e88bde38e0
msgid "Goals"
msgstr ""

#: bd5e24a057cf49d38cf513cdaf86c20c
msgid ""
"Make installed artifacts derive from one auditable package and resource "
"manifest."
msgstr ""

#: a5d04511326c49c9aada536d3415b7c6
msgid ""
"Use conventional Python domain packages whose physical module paths "
"express ownership."
msgstr ""

#: 813d28de3c7b48c5a9f34d55245a43a9
msgid "Separate reusable Torch compatibility from project-specific integrations."
msgstr ""

#: 1818cf6a0e904cb798a5f508a6ce842e
msgid ""
"Move tests, examples, tools, benchmarks, and documentation out of the "
"runtime package unless they are required after installation."
msgstr ""

#: a37c78c94615448497f8d0a63eb9b249
msgid ""
"Turn correctness, packaging, lint, and performance requirements into "
"automated gates."
msgstr ""

#: f94c0313ac584906a7820504a4e6be3a
msgid ""
"Preserve Jittor's JIT runtime resource paths and public import "
"compatibility throughout the migration."
msgstr ""

#: 5d9226fe84a54d5fb67f20defa99a971
msgid "Non-goals"
msgstr ""

#: 533b5e5be5e4461f8dbc55e28806de26
msgid ""
"Replacing Jittor's meta-operator or unified graph design with PyTorch "
"internals."
msgstr ""

#: ea156f9a9ee94a8aa0f2d938a923ba0d
msgid ""
"Moving runtime C++/CUDA resources merely to make the source tree look "
"uniform."
msgstr ""

#: 3d59b389f7db485d962d993a98848ea5
msgid "Claiming backend capability from import or structure tests alone."
msgstr ""

#: 7d2839d6d3c24054ba0e0625cc27be06
msgid ""
"Keeping every historical reflection path forever. Where a deliberate "
"public metadata change is made, old serialized artifacts receive an "
"explicit compatibility path and a migration test."
msgstr ""

#: b051a85a497b42b083d9a5d5ea57c621
msgid "Hard Path Invariants"
msgstr ""

#: 04697cd11f4944d7bb6ac0ef744627db
msgid ""
"`python/jittor` is the runtime `jittor_path`, not only a Python package. "
"The following paths remain physically stable unless the compiler contract"
" is first changed and independently validated:"
msgstr ""

#: 3232523452b2426c8694322af47bcbcb
msgid ""
"`python/jittor/src/**`, including extensionless resources and the source "
"files selected by compiler ordering rules;"
msgstr ""

#: 245bf2d238e44a73acb32d44222444b2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`python/jittor/extern/**`, including the `<backend>/{inc,ops,src}` layout"
" and ACL filename dispatch conventions;"
msgstr ""

#: 1d8d0f3f2654462c9a40a5750eb391ad
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`python/jittor/utils/{dlink_compiler.py,dumpdef.py}`;"
msgstr ""

#: 01410ede03f740efade5f4eb1076f19c
msgid "`python/jittor/math_util/src/*.h`;"
msgstr ""

#: 70abb08f7a894ebdbea3aa44687dd141
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`python/jittor/compat/shim/cpp_extension/{include,src}/**` as the "
"canonical installed ABI resource boundary for extension builds;"
msgstr ""

#: 57f2504455054a00a0e116f437d5f152
msgid ""
"`python/jittor/other/code_softmax.py` while the CUDA fast path loads it "
"by filesystem location;"
msgstr ""

#: f834ca717a6c4d268048ff849ce96833
msgid "`python/jittor_utils` as a sibling of `python/jittor`;"
msgstr ""

#: 75858fba183741fea811cfc0cff4e7f4
msgid ""
"the literal `__version__ = '...'` assignment in "
"`python/jittor/__init__.py` while release and cache readers still parse "
"it directly."
msgstr ""

#: 6373e8bb9ba74dec90a3b4a2127e8bfd
msgid ""
"These invariants are checked as runtime contracts. They are not "
"exemptions from packaging completeness: every installed resource required"
" by those contracts must be present in the wheel."
msgstr ""

#: 5a0b6fc297e2428cb87f89c04165556a
msgid "Target Layout"
msgstr ""

#: d220dd81cd1b41ed9f698ecb8294d009
msgid ""
"The tree is a destination, not authorization for a flag-day move. Each "
"migration must leave the repository buildable and preserve the hard path "
"invariants."
msgstr ""

#: 0a70fa57cd5045e2a6258a71d3b91b1c
msgid "Decision 1: Domain Packages"
msgstr ""

#: ae62da17df334e6dbcd1735a4f3fa85f
msgid ""
"Stage 3 converged `nn.py + _nn/`, `misc.py + _misc/`, `pool.py + _pool/`,"
" and `torch_compat.py + _torch_compat/` to the normal `nn/`, `misc/`, "
"`pool/`, and `compat/torch/` packages. The following rules are the "
"resulting contract."
msgstr ""

#: a1237a404cca43698c32da4147e3409c
msgid "A domain package's `__init__.py` is its composition and re-export surface."
msgstr ""

#: 3a2ea1c9ed5f4ba4a9063337fe258134
msgid ""
"Implementations live under meaningful paths such as `nn.modules.conv` and"
" `nn.functional.padding`."
msgstr ""

#: 5dd8e37e75b94fcb951dbdc223e75b31
msgid ""
"Implementations may import the initialized domain interfaces they "
"actually depend on. The end state does not contain duplicated "
"`_JittorRuntimeProxy` service locators."
msgstr ""

#: 80ad57b177f84881bbe3fde75037cd10
msgid ""
"Callable metadata reports the real implementation module, matching "
"mainstream Python library practice. New code does not recursively rewrite"
" `__module__` to hide ownership."
msgstr ""

#: 7c2fcec7b29646efbadc275f8c55e9b7
msgid "Historical imports such as `from jittor import nn` remain valid."
msgstr ""

#: d32e9acb48c34eb392aeadac2943955e
msgid ""
"Pickle compatibility is verified against fixtures made before the move. "
"Compatibility aliases or a narrowly scoped unpickling mapping are "
"retained only where an old artifact cannot otherwise load."
msgstr ""

#: f19b9c23a7a3486a8cca1851e7b7387f
msgid ""
"Backend post-processing and monkeypatch points become explicit registries"
" or documented extension hooks, not accidental mutation of facade "
"globals."
msgstr ""

#: ef85abe7c25a4be29a0322f0f4728779
msgid ""
"The four Stage 3 facade/private-package pairs and the later FSDP2 "
"migration scaffold no longer exist. The maintained Torch API lives in "
"`jittor.compat.torch`, FSDP2 support lives in `jittor.compat.fsdp2`, and "
"deployment and import patching live in `jittor.compat.shim`. No new "
"domain may adopt a facade/private-package pairing."
msgstr ""
"阶段 3 的四组 facade/私有包，以及后续的 FSDP2 迁移脚手架均已移除。维护中的 Torch API 位于 "
"`jittor.compat.torch`，FSDP2 支持位于 `jittor.compat.fsdp2`，部署和导入修补位于 "
"`jittor.compat.shim`。任何新领域都不得采用 facade/私有包配对。"

#: 9eeecaf3d8f342f7be84ba8dc5cf012f
msgid "Canonical And Legacy Imports"
msgstr ""

#: a428291021064f7088bc63591317c3c3
msgid "The physical target and compatibility entry points are:"
msgstr ""

#: fd52d49e4b2b4cefac642b9178cce858
msgid "Canonical implementation"
msgstr ""

#: 49163ebc605b4caca5489c746451955d
msgid "Compatibility entry point"
msgstr ""

#: 5b32d7d8dd24422989397a9d86d0d0e1
msgid "`jittor.nn` package"
msgstr ""

#: 1a7e6e3056af4f39a2c8f3128c1c102b
msgid "existing `from jittor import nn`"
msgstr ""

#: 6e1bd9447bda49d19933f05b49d56835
msgid "`jittor.compat.torch`"
msgstr ""

#: a6b2ca1c681e40969ea5b325019f3cbe
msgid "`jittor.torch_compat`"
msgstr ""

#: 20f9925388694e6cacb9c07304297a83
msgid "`jittor.compat.shim`"
msgstr ""

#: d40f955d59784880b976be3a77bb79cf
msgid "`jittor.torch_shim` and deployed `torch` aliases"
msgstr ""

#: efa691abfca3482c9ea5d6a3ef698dca
msgid "`jittor.compat.fsdp2`"
msgstr ""

#: d5b66df73bac4b1b99a2fa1bdcf93170
msgid "`jittor.torch_fsdp2_compat`"
msgstr ""

#: dd0411faa1cf408585ef9084292b4e1b
msgid "`jittor.compat.triton`"
msgstr ""

#: 42c91b2107d64bb28aa8e243db273e87
msgid "`jittor.triton_shim`"
msgstr ""

#: 1a277b254a9943818bab225cbe522c69
msgid ""
"Compatibility paths must resolve to the canonical objects and must not "
"run a second installer. Where callers can observe `sys.modules` identity "
"today, the migration preserves one shared module object rather than "
"parallel facades with copied state."
msgstr ""

#: 4b38786dc1564ff887197928ae0060b4
msgid ""
"`jittor.nn.functional` becomes a physical package and remains the "
"canonical object registered as `torch.nn.functional` when the Torch shim "
"is active. The conversion must remove the current dynamic-module "
"constructor without allowing the shim to overwrite the package or "
"duplicate registrations."
msgstr ""

#: 0b88ee94126a464ca8c75d6ab268e370
msgid "Decision 2: Four Compatibility Layers"
msgstr ""

#: 226cc69462314d7581b290f4414a590c
msgid ""
"Torch compatibility is separated by ownership rather than downstream "
"project:"
msgstr ""

#: e340838dfa4244e5983d2117e06f4958
msgid ""
"**Framework capability** belongs in Jittor domains. Examples include "
"parameterized attention, RoPE, normalization, mesh, and production sparse"
" convolution operations."
msgstr ""

#: 0a755346602f4953850f34aae4eb7da0
msgid ""
"**Reusable mechanism** belongs in `jittor.compat`. A registry-based "
"module patcher owns import timing and restoration; a parameterized "
"external-backend loader owns source discovery, manifests, builds, and "
"cache identity."
msgstr ""

#: 35fb5f6f6570472d86b6fd103e621f2e
msgid ""
"**Jittor root-cause fixes** belong in core semantics. Tensor gradient "
"state, `Parameter` identity, and shape hashability must not be papered "
"over in each downstream library."
msgstr ""

#: 6e502f6174cb40cf853193fbc58c40bd
msgid ""
"**Project/version glue** lives in optional integration distributions such"
" as `jittor-trellis`, `jittor-gs`, and `jittor-hf-compat`, registered "
"through entry points. Mainline Jittor does not install a permanent "
"TRELLIS or Gaussian Splatting finder for every process."
msgstr ""

#: fa0bc788782b479383237e035fd5e752
msgid ""
"Installers must report each attempted patch independently. A broad "
"`try/except Exception: pass` around a chain of patches is forbidden "
"because one failure otherwise hides all later compatibility work."
msgstr ""

#: 5f9aea25218f4700be33116dc7ca7a33
msgid "Packaging Boundary"
msgstr ""

#: 269fbbc68fb24b5eb1dc07a4d8b303d0
msgid ""
"`pyproject.toml` is the authoritative project metadata and build-system "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#: 9a4d8faf64674c02a0f455b630dbe9ea
msgid ""
"Package discovery includes every directory under `python/` that contains "
"an `__init__.py`; a structure test compares the filesystem and build "
"metadata."
msgstr ""

#: 7ccad35ff2b543e0b0e6c7f08f2bdd15
msgid ""
"Runtime non-Python resources are declared explicitly through "
"`MANIFEST.in` and package-data configuration. Recursive catch-all globs "
"are not used to smuggle undeclared packages into a wheel."
msgstr ""

#: f24fa97cd54c4f508f25c8d01195a131
msgid ""
"Tests, demos, notebooks, release utilities, and benchmarks are not wheel "
"payload unless a documented installed command requires them."
msgstr ""

#: 4ad91468cf0349f8a90c8e4849dbc194
msgid ""
"`jittor.selftest` is the small installed smoke test used by install "
"scripts and container health checks."
msgstr ""

#: 4615e53149a3438bb169d199b92e5d39
msgid ""
"Every packaging change is checked by a member SHA-256 plus exact-path "
"wheel baseline. Additions, content changes, and removals require reviewed"
" hashes or path allowances, and every allowance must be consumed by the "
"candidate so a stale wheel cannot silently pass by reverting an approved "
"transition."
msgstr ""

#: 8aa40aa9322848f5bcd2fd986a08ce58
msgid "Test Boundary"
msgstr ""

#: 9f9fa45a73a14429b4aca5b0a8a97c95
msgid ""
"The repository test suite lives under top-level `tests/` and is collected"
" by pytest. It is not an installed `jittor` subpackage. Existing "
"`unittest.TestCase` tests remain valid under pytest and were not "
"rewritten merely for the move."
msgstr ""

#: 4891dbebff984df88d927ecff8188967
msgid ""
"The migration inventory was reconciled from the original 233-module "
"estimate to 239 top-level test modules. Its 123 cross-test edges across "
"76 files were replaced with explicit helpers derived from the actual "
"graph; all 239 modules received a recorded destination rather than "
"relying on the older partial category estimate."
msgstr ""

#: 4cb9893972244b748074577f4cd901b4
msgid ""
"Shared test utilities live in `tests/_helpers/`; test modules do not "
"import one another as an implicit helper API."
msgstr ""

#: 63da6d763df54bc5bc5bd3687c3e157c
msgid "Structure, CPU, CUDA, and NPU suites are separate CI layers."
msgstr ""

#: ff2572049ad14a5cbfd3bef1b9e3df36
msgid "Test selection uses names and markers, never `listdir()` positions."
msgstr ""

#: 123068b71ee5448c9377cf90a31ba7a5
msgid ""
"The C++ `test.h` resource lives with its compiler include consumers under"
" `python/jittor/src/utils/`."
msgstr ""

#: a0f0246cacf24d9aa62efcadd59d34f2
msgid ""
"Installed-environment checks use `jittor.selftest`, not a shipped test "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: 84ef627eff3345d585514c120fec0078
msgid "Tool And Example Boundary"
msgstr ""

#: d5858aea4eeb4662a7f558588855977e
msgid ""
"Repository-operated commands live under top-level `tools/`; teaching and "
"runnable samples live under `examples/`. Neither tree contains "
"`__init__.py` or participates in runtime package discovery. They are "
"included in the source distribution for maintainers, but direct and "
"sdist-derived wheels exclude them."
msgstr ""

#: be62a8200fc74c2dbed96cc8017e1a89
msgid ""
"Stage 6 retires the published `jittor.vcompiler` package as a deliberate "
"Jittor 2.0 breaking change. It compiled a private C++ extension during "
"import, had no supported in-repository consumer, and has no direct "
"replacement; custom operator authors should use the maintained "
"`compile_custom_op` and `compile_custom_ops` interfaces instead. The "
"package-local `version` file is also retired because project metadata and"
" `jittor.__version__` are the version authorities."
msgstr ""

#: 0d48a692c58e4fe69408a5b9a1a10d2a
msgid ""
"Stage 6 retires the old LLVM alignment pass and the unused "
"`compiler.compile_extern()` build hook together. The active compiler startup"
" did not call that hook; keeping a private pass tied to LLVM compiler "
"internals added an unsupported distribution payload without affecting the "
"runtime JIT path. The normal Clang cold import, forward/backward graph, and "
"custom JIT regressions remain the acceptance gate for the supported compiler"
" path."
msgstr ""
"阶段 6 同时退役旧 LLVM 对齐 pass 和未使用的 `compiler.compile_extern()` "
"构建钩子。当前编译器启动流程不会调用该钩子；保留一个绑定 LLVM 编译器内部实现的"
"私有 pass，只会增加不受支持的发行内容，而不会影响运行时 JIT 路径。正常的 Clang "
"冷启动导入、前后向图和自定义 JIT 回归仍是受支持编译器路径的验收门禁。"

#: 03c91e828a7f412f8d1b2eee0ef4316b
msgid "Tooling And Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: 324e64a230e0423aba6274b92709b5d3
msgid ""
"Ruff supplies formatting and linting; mypy is introduced with an "
"explicit, ratcheted scope rather than an unmaintainable all-at-once "
"exception list."
msgstr ""

#: 2c196e60f1684286ad8ca59ef8b8e833
msgid ""
"Pre-commit runs fast deterministic checks, while nox is the canonical "
"local and CI command entry point."
msgstr ""

#: 5521da922ec8456bb6653454337b4903
msgid ""
"`.github/ci-baseline.env` is the single maintained definition for the "
"host runner, Python version, CPU CI image, CUDA requirement, hardware "
"runner labels, container matrix, and release validation matrix. The "
"reusable `_ci-baseline.yml` workflow exports those values; individual "
"workflows consume its outputs instead of restating versions or runner "
"labels."
msgstr ""
"`.github/ci-baseline.env` 是宿主 runner、Python 版本、CPU CI 镜像、CUDA "
"要求、硬件 runner 标签、容器矩阵和发行验证矩阵的唯一维护定义。可复用工作流 "
"`_ci-baseline.yml` 负责导出这些值；各工作流使用其输出，不再重复声明版本或 "
"runner 标签。"

#: 7fa082405fd54cd786a91ba52445e3d4
msgid ""
"CPU tests and packaging run in the CPU image from that baseline. CUDA and"
" NPU jobs are a formal exception to container parity: they run on labeled"
" self-hosted hosts because the device, driver, toolkit, and vendor "
"runtime are host capabilities. macOS and Windows release checks are the "
"corresponding native-platform exception. These jobs still consume the "
"common Python, toolkit, runner-label, or platform-matrix values that "
"apply to them."
msgstr ""
"CPU 测试和打包任务使用该基线指定的 CPU 镜像。CUDA 和 NPU 任务是容器一致性规则的正式例外："
"设备、驱动、工具链和厂商运行时属于宿主能力，因此这些任务在带标签的自托管宿主上运行。macOS "
"和 Windows 发行检查是相应的原生平台例外。这些任务仍使用适用于自身的公共 Python、工具链、"
"runner 标签或平台矩阵配置。"

#: bcd658dd5a8544d1ad6123dcbfd1e2e2
msgid ""
"Releases use `python -m build` and PyPI trusted publishing. Jittor ships "
"Python plus JIT source resources rather than a prebuilt platform "
"extension, so its one canonical wheel remains `py3-none-any`. The release"
" builds that wheel once and installs the same artifact on Linux, macOS, "
"and Windows. The cibuildwheel checks assert that a platform wheel is "
"*not* produced; they do not replace the canonical wheel with three "
"platform-specific wheels."
msgstr ""
"发行流程使用 `python -m build` 和 PyPI 可信发布。Jittor 分发 Python 代码与 JIT "
"源码资源，而不是预编译的平台扩展，因此唯一的规范 wheel 保持为 `py3-none-any`。发行流程只构建一次该 "
"wheel，并在 Linux、macOS 和 Windows 上安装同一产物。cibuildwheel 检查用于断言不会生成平台 "
"wheel，而不是用三个平台专用 wheel 取代规范 wheel。"

#: 8cb4040d37414577af41aaab04b68d2a
msgid ""
"ASV tracks speed and memory by commit using `--python=same`, selected "
"revisions, a Jittor cache isolated from unit tests, and externally stored"
" results and HTML reports."
msgstr ""
"ASV 使用 `--python=same`、选定的修订版本、与单元测试隔离的 Jittor 缓存，以及存储在源码树外部的"
"结果和 HTML 报告，按提交追踪速度与内存。"

#: 8a3c18f11555414dae001677b165aa88
msgid ""
"Documentation uses Sphinx, MyST, standard gettext/sphinx-intl "
"localization, and jupytext-managed tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: 8ed250521acd4758bf8e15a7688a3334
msgid "Migration Order"
msgstr ""

#: c6c7f88a4e324f8cbe5db2f57f10a614
msgid "Record this RFC and supersede conflicting architecture rules."
msgstr ""

#: 3279f28cb7e44bf2bd3430ef9383b2ee
msgid "Make packaging complete and establish an immutable wheel-content baseline."
msgstr ""

#: fe523bc56eb041e29235ebd2a1f76ca6
msgid "Add tooling, CI, release, container, and performance infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: d66323cba3834c90878ab6df2fa138cd
msgid "Convert domain facade/private pairs into domain packages."
msgstr ""

#: d514104cf0a54f8ab15f1fbf8649a419
msgid "Separate compatibility capability, mechanism, root-cause fixes, and glue."
msgstr ""

#: 80fb09ccf4814b1dbcd9548ba25cc343
